    "status": "stub",
    "notes": "Not from an official source, which is the point: these are widely used but locally variable, so the UI always pairs them with the local-guidance note. Stays status=stub for that reason. Entries duplicated by the HQ-approved list were dropped so HQ wins. A trailing parenthetical was treated as an annotation and stripped (A1-A9 lost '(Directorate)'), except where stripping would collide -- ASOR-L and ASOR-S keep '(Long)' and '(Short)' because that gloss is the only thing telling them apart. Case-variant abbreviations (Qtr/qtr, QTRLY/QTR) are all kept so recognition matches whichever a writer used; replacement picks one deterministically. REVIEW: the platform designators (F-15 Eagle, MQ-9 Reaper, AIM-9 Sidewinder, ...) map a name to a designator rather than a phrase to its abbreviation, so greedy replacement will rewrite any use of the word 'Eagle' or 'Reaper'. Prune them if that is not wanted."
  },
